    "title": "Soap actor Patrick Muldoon has died suddenly at 57, was he married, did he have kids?",
    "text": "Patrick Muldoon who starred in primetime soap Melrose Place has died at 57.Actor and producer Patrick Muldoon who starred in Melrose Place, daytime drama Days of Our Lives and movie Starship Troopers, has died at 57 following a heart attack. Only two days ago, the actor had taken to Instagram to post about his latest project.Fans have now responded to his post with tributes to the actor. One wrote: “Grew up watching you in starship troopers . R.I.P legend.” Another person said: “You will be missed! Wishing all of Patrick's friends, family and devoted fans love, comfort and intentions of peace and ease.”After he graduated, Patrick Muldoon starred on Saved by the Bell. The Instagram page for Saved By The Bell Fever wrote: “RIP Patrick Muldoon, famously known as Jeff from Saved by the Bell. We’re grateful that we had the chance to show him our appreciation on this page not too long ago. Our thoughts are with his family during this time.” Soap actor Patrick Muldoon has died suddenly at 57, was he married, did he have kids? Photo: Getty Images | Getty ImagesThere is also another post which reads: “RIP Patrick Muldoon. 1968-2026. Thanks for the memories, Jeff. 💔”In September last year, Patrick Muldoon wrote about Oasis on Instagram and said: “Ok. I am an @oasis head if you can’t tell. I spent the early 2000’s trying to sing like @liamgallagher and write like @noelgallagherfansclub #legend they were better last night than when i saw them 20 years ago! #rocknroll #oasis.”Patrick Muldoon appeared on Days of Our Lives as the character of Austin Reed, he first played the part of Austin from 1992 until 1995 and then reprised the role for a year in 2011. He also starred as Richard Hart on Melrose Place and played Zander Barcalow in the movie Starship Troopers which came out in 1997.Patrick Muldoon was not only an actor but also produced the likes of The Tribes of Palos Verdes, The Card Counter and most recently Kockroach which is currently filming. Kockroach stars the likes of Chris Hemsworth and Taron Egerton. Patrick Muldoon was not married, but had a partner Miriam Rothbart, he is survived by her, as well as his parents Deanna and Patrick Muldoon Sr. and his sister and brother-in-law, Shana and Ahmet Zappa. Patrick Muldoon did not have children. According to reports Patrick Muldoon died suddenly at 57 following a heart attack.",
